# Cursor agent — universal standards

1. **Route first:** read **`docs/WORKFLOW_ROUTER.md`** in this repo (foundation + [pstack](https://cursor.com/marketplace/cursor/pstack) + Matt skills — no duplicate pre-build).
2. **Details:** **`docs/CURSOR_AGENT_STANDARDS.md`**. Other `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` here add product/stack rules on top.

## Quick rules

- **Tier A:** one sentence + fix; no grill, no pre-build, skip `/poteto-mode` unless user asks.
- **Tier B+ + pstack active** (`/poteto-mode` or pstack skill this turn): follow playbook; **skip** foundation pre-build block; still run **grill-with-docs** / **improve-codebase-architecture** when router Step 3 triggers.
- **Tier B+ + no pstack:** foundation pre-build + human **go** when behaviour/contracts change.
- **Tier C:** **grill-with-docs** before code; then `/poteto-mode` or `/architect with checkpoint`.
- **Parallel work:** one lead; handoff brief if multiple implementers share a seam.
- **Done:** lint/tests; **commit, push, deploy** if repo documents how (**ask** if unknown).
